{
 "_comment": "The index-run census as the client's two doctor rows (nexus.health._check_stale_indexing_runs and _check_failed_runs_hidden_chunks, run as a doctor run runs them over the live walk) and the engine route GET /v1/catalog/index-run/census both compute it; tests/catalog/test_index_run_census_cases.py runs this table through the client rows and IndexRunCensusParityTest runs it through the route, so a change to either side's rule on what this table varies fails one of the two. 'now' is the clock both halves are held to. WHAT IT PINS. stale: a document is stale when its fence is 'indexing' and index_started_at is 6 h or more before now (inclusive; none recorded is not stale; other states and tombstones never are); notes counts the stale documents of content type knowledge (the client counts their distinct names, source_uri else the tumbler, and a live document's name is unique). fence: checked (documents carrying a state), reported_null, undated_reported_null, floor_candidates (no state, indexed_at strictly after the floor, 2026-08-07T16:00:35Z), the baseline (the earliest indexed_at among COMPLETE documents that share an index_run_id with a second document that has a usable indexed_at, else the earliest indexed_at of any COMPLETE document; an indexing or failed document never dates it) and post_anchor (unstamped documents indexed strictly after both the floor and the baseline), named by source_uri. failed_hidden: of the failed documents (tombstones excepted), those the heal would rebuild: no manifest row, a content hash (metadata.content_hash, else index_content_hash) and a registered collection, with n >= 1 chunk rows of that collection carrying the hash and chunk_count 0 or n <= chunk_count. 'documents' hold every column the rows read; 'collections' are the registered ones and 'chunk_groups' the chunk rows carrying a content_hash. WHAT IT DOES NOT PIN (Java tests only): the limit and its capped flag, tenants, the partial index, timeouts, the clients' run-id ledger and candidate caps (5,000 and 1,000), a non-string content_hash.",
